    "qualifying_subset_targets": [],
    "qualifying_subset_size": 0,
    "subset_rule": "A target qualifies only if its own transcript falls significantly in BOTH screens AND its transcriptome-wide response profiles correlate at Pearson >= 0.30 between screens.  Five qualifying targets would be the minimum for a subset answer.",
    "threshold_provenance": "POST_HOC_DESCRIPTIVE, NOT A PROSPECTIVE FREEZE.  These cuts were chosen after the statistics were computed and are stated so the verdict is reproducible, not because they carry independent authority.  The verdict does not depend on them: the highest per-target Pearson observed anywhere is 0.2117, so C2 fails for every threshold above that; the jointly engaged count is 1 of 31, so C1 fails for every threshold above 0.032; and C5 is a design fact, not a measured quantity.",
    "answer_scope": "NO for transcriptome-wide perturbation-response benchmarking on this pair.  Not 'only for a subset' either: 0 target(s) satisfy both the engagement and the profile-concordance requirement, against a minimum of 5.",
    "decisive_reasons": [
      "Target engagement is not demonstrated: 3/31 targets in iTF and 3/31 in iPSC significantly reduce their own transcript (FDR<0.05, Log2FC<0); 1 target(s) in both.",
      "Continuous concordance over shared targets is near zero: pooled Pearson 0.0723, Spearman 0.0438, median per-target Pearson 0.0277, pooled sign agreement 0.5181 against a 0.50 coin flip.",
      "What agreement exists is one target, not a weak broad signal: 50 of the 54 jointly significant rows come from ZNF644; 28 of 31 shared targets have no jointly significant readout gene at all.",
      "Non-replication is not only a power problem.  Of 800 rows significant in iTF but not iPSC, 223 are formally inconsistent between the two screens (|z_diff|>1.96), and of 54 rows significant in BOTH screens, 50 are formally inconsistent.  Low power explains part of the gap; the screens also actively contradict each other.",
      "The pair is not independent replication: NOT INDEPENDENT REPLICATION.  Same lab, same publication, same sgRNA library (row-for-row identical feature reference), same vector, same parental line, same analysis pipeline, same non-targeting control design.  The pair is a within-study protocol contrast, not a between-study replication."
    ],
    "what_is_still_usable": [
      "Target identity is resolvable: 30 of 31 shared target symbols carry a deposited Ensembl-anchored protospacer.",
      "The tables remain valid as an exposure-free covariate source (which genes were targeted, with which guides, in which cell models) and as a negative control: a model must not be rewarded for reproducing them."
    ],
    "measurement_failure_vs_biological_disagreement": "BOTH, AND THEY CANNOT BE FULLY SEPARATED WITH THE DEPOSITED DATA.  Per-target cell counts, guide-level counts and per-cell detection are not deposited, so the power side can only be bounded through the standard errors implied by each screen's own p-values.  Under that reconstruction a majority of the iTF-only hits are consistent with insufficient power in iPSC, but a substantial minority, and most of the jointly significant rows, are formally inconsistent.  Neither 'the screens disagree biologically' nor 'the screens are merely underpowered' is established alone; the honest statement is that the deposit cannot separate them, and that either one disqualifies the pair as a truth standard."
  },
